Z||000006||stimpy||08-22-2000||08:11 PM||||Funny you should mention Neon's. This morning driving to work, sedate 75 mph in the fast lane, very light traffic, when I see the telltale headlights f a Neon pokin up behhind me, then veering over to the full right lanes to try to pass. I can see this buttmunch is going to ill himself trying to get by on the right so I downshift and hammer down to about 88 mph, turning him into a speck.  As I get off at the next exit, I slow down as the hi-po is issuing a ticket in the breakdown lane. Sure enough, this backward hat wearin, 18" wheel ridin, fartcan muffler wearin neon does the fly-by to get off in front of me, AND FLIPPED ME OFF! This is the gratitude I get for getting out of his way. I don't condone road rage, but sometimes I can understand it...<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||08-22-2000||09:33 PM||||Dont down neons guys. There are two models in specific that in know will crack a stock v-6 fiero. The ACR and the R/T.  My buddy has an acr (american cup racing) neon that runs 13.2's all day long in the 1/4 with no forced induction. Low 13's all motor. His car has absolutly no options. It came radio delete from the factory, no ac, no heater, manual winows and locks, no bumper reinforcements, ultra-lite wheels with slicks. He could have gotten an option roll cage from crysler, but he thought that it would add weight. He's all about being light. it's 12:1 and i dont know if any of you have heard a 12:1 4 banger lately, but they're wicked loud!  The durability of a neon isn't theyre though. If you race one enough it's bound to break something. He has a pile of half shafts sitting in his garage in peices. and 2 transmissions with holes in them beside those.<P> I've raced a r/t on the street before with exhuast and ignition mods, and i beat him out of the hole, but he caught up and passed me at the end of the 1/4 mile. He wasn't stock either though. intake and exhuast mods i beleive. It would be a very close race between two stockers, altough sorry to say i think the neon would have the advantage. I mean neons weight about absolutly nothing.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||08-23-2000||12:38 AM||||13.2?????? are you sure?  I had a r/t neon tell me to "take my $hit home" Because he kept doing fly-by's on me.  I think if he ever would have raced me off the line it would have ben alll over for him, but he was a ricer punk so of course he never did....<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
